<article class="env-lemma" id="02V6">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/02V6">Lemma <span data-tag="02V6">29.44.9</span>.</a> A base change of a (locally) projective morphism is (locally) projective. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      This is true because the base change of a projective bundle over a scheme is a projective bundle, the pullback of a finite type $\mathcal{O}$-module is of finite type (Modules, Lemma <a href="/tag/01B6" data-tag="01B6">17.9.2</a>) and the fact that the base change of a closed immersion is a closed immersion, see Schemes, Lemma <a href="/tag/01JY" data-tag="01JY">26.18.2</a>. Some details omitted. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>